.TH OSM 1 "2026-08-12" "osm" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
osm \- send encrypted messages through any chat, using published SSH keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B osm send
.RI [ user "[@" host "][:" fingerprint-prefix "]] [" message ]
.br
.B osm read
.RI [ file ]
.br
.B osm keys
.RI  user [@ host ]
.br
.B osm doctor
.br
.B osm version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B osm
encrypts a short secret to a recipient identified by their account on a code
forge, using the SSH public key that account already publishes. The recipient
decrypts with the private key they already hold. Nothing is exchanged in
advance and no keyserver is involved.
.PP
The output is an inert armored block. It is never a shell command, so a
tampered paste cannot execute code on the recipient's machine.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B send
Encrypt to one or more recipients. Reads the message on standard input when no
message argument is given, which keeps it out of the process list.
.TP
.B read
Decrypt. Reads standard input when piped, a file when given one, and otherwise
the clipboard.
.TP
.B keys
List the keys osm can encrypt to for an account, with fingerprints.
.TP
.B doctor
Report the state of every dependency and print a remedy for each failure.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-to " target"
Add a recipient. Repeat for several.
.TP
.BI \-\-keys\-file " path"
Add recipients from a local public key file.
.TP
.BI \-\-key " prefix"
Encrypt to one key only, chosen by fingerprint prefix.
.TP
.BI \-\-sign " user"
Sign as a user whose published key you hold.
.TP
.B \-\-accept\-new\-key
Accept a recipient whose pinned fingerprints changed.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print machine readable output.
.TP
.B \-\-qr
Print the message as a QR code instead of text.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-clipboard
Do not copy the result to the clipboard.
.TP
.BI \-\-identity " path"
Decrypt with a specific private key.
.TP
.B \-\-clipboard
Read the message from the clipboard.
.TP
.B \-\-require\-signature
Refuse a message that carries no signature.
.SH HOSTS
.B github
is the default.
.BR gitlab ,
.B codeberg
and
.B sourcehut
are known. Any other value is treated as a self-hosted forge serving
.IR host / user .keys.
Bitbucket publishes no public key endpoint, so use
.B \-\-keys\-file
for it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OSM_MIN_RSA_BITS
Minimum RSA key size before a warning. Default 3072.
.TP
.B OSM_CLIPBOARD_TIMEOUT
Seconds before the clipboard is cleared. 0 disables. Default 90.
.TP
.B OSM_HTTP_TIMEOUT
Seconds before a key fetch times out. Default 10.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where pinned recipient fingerprints are stored. Defaults to ~/.config.
.SH SECURITY
An unsigned message is confidential but anonymous. Anyone can encrypt to a
public key and claim to be anyone. Sign with
.B \-\-sign
so the recipient can verify, or refuse unsigned messages with
.BR \-\-require\-signature .
.PP
The forge is the trust anchor. osm pins the fingerprints it saw on first
contact and refuses to send if they change, so an account takeover is loud
rather than silent.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success, non-zero on any failure. No plaintext is printed when a
signature fails to verify.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR age (1),
.BR ssh-keygen (1)
